window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-e3c5173f4c4c14ef"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"codex-sdk\">Codex SDK</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code> 可获取对应 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>如果你通过 Codex CLI、IDE 扩展或 Codex 云端使用 Codex，也可以通过 SDK（软件开发工具包）在程序中控制它。可以把 SDK 理解为一组让你在自己的代码中调用 Codex 的接口。</p> <p>在以下情况下可以使用 SDK：</p> <ul> <li>将 Codex 纳入 CI/CD（持续集成/持续交付或部署）流水线；</li> <li>创建能够调用 Codex 来完成复杂工程任务的自有智能体；</li> <li>将 Codex 集成到内部工具和工作流中；</li> <li>将 Codex 集成到你自己的应用程序中。</li> </ul> <p>可以使用 Codex SDK 自动执行编码任务，包括 CI 中的作业。若要构建自定义客户端来处理身份验证、对话历史、审批和流式智能体事件，请使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-341246db376ea9e1\">Codex app-server</a>。</p> <p><code>codex mcp-server</code> 命令和独立的 <code>codex-mcp-server</code> 二进制文件已移除。现有集成请改用 <a href=\"#/article/a-341246db376ea9e1\">Codex app-server</a>。</p> <p>如果你拥有 Beta 访问权限，并且需要针对代码库或更改进行扫描，同时获得结构化安全发现和覆盖情况，请使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-13b97f7316a6bfd5\">Codex Security TypeScript SDK</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"typescript-library\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"typescript\">TypeScript 库</h2> <p>TypeScript 库可以让你的应用程序启动、继续和恢复本地 Codex 线程。</p> <p>请在服务器端使用此库；它要求 Node.js 18 或更高版本。</p> <p><a id=\"installation\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_1\">安装</h3> <p>首先通过 <code>npm</code> 安装 Codex SDK：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @openai/codex-sdk\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"usage\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_2\">用法</h3> <p>启动一个 Codex 线程，并通过提示运行它。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-ts\">\n\nconst codex = new Codex();\nconst thread = codex.startThread();\nconst result = await thread.run(\n  \"Make a plan to diagnose and fix the CI failures\"\n);\n\nconsole.log(result.finalResponse);\n</code></pre> <p>再次调用 <code>run()</code> 可在同一线程中继续；提供线程 ID 则可以恢复过去的线程。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-ts\">// running the same thread\nconst result = await thread.run(\"Implement the plan\");\n\nconsole.log(result.finalResponse);\n\n// resuming past thread\n\nconst threadId = \"&lt;thread-id&gt;\";\nconst thread2 = codex.resumeThread(threadId);\nconst result2 = await thread2.run(\"Pick up where you left off\");\n\nconsole.log(result2.finalResponse);\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"configuration-overrides\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_3\">配置覆盖</h3> <p>使用 <code>config</code> 设置结构化的 Codex 配置。对于无法用点分隔路径表达的键，可使用 <code>configOverrides</code> 传入原始 TOML 字符串；每个字符串会作为单独的 <code>--config</code> 参数传递：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-ts\">const codex = new Codex({\n  config: { default_permissions: \"audit\" },\n  configOverrides: [\n    'permissions.audit.filesystem={\":root\"=\"read\",\"/path/to/project/.env\"=\"deny\"}',\n  ],\n});\n</code></pre> <p>原始覆盖项的优先级高于结构化 <code>config</code>。随后，SDK 会应用 <code>baseUrl</code> 等受管理设置以及线程专属选项；这些设置的优先级高于前两者。使用这些覆盖项不会修改你的 Codex 配置文件。</p> <p>更多详情请参阅 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/tree/main/sdk/typescript\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TypeScript 代码库（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"python-library\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"python\">Python 库</h2> <p>Python SDK 通过 JSON-RPC（基于 JSON 消息的远程过程调用协议）控制本地 Codex app-server。它要求 Python 3.10 或更高版本。已发布的 SDK 构建版本包含固定版本的 Codex CLI 运行时依赖项。</p> <p><a id=\"installation_1\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">安装</h3> <p>运行以下命令安装 SDK：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">pip install openai-codex\n</code></pre> <p>已发布的 SDK 构建版本会自动使用其固定版本的运行时。只有在你有意指定某个本地 Codex 可执行文件时，才传入 <code>CodexConfig(codex_bin=...)</code>。</p> <p>Python SDK 已作为稳定版本发布。<code>pip install openai-codex</code> 会安装最新稳定版本；使用 <code>pip install --pre openai-codex</code> 可选择安装较新的预发布版本。</p> <p><a id=\"usage_1\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_5\">用法</h3> <p>启动 Codex、创建线程并运行提示。以下示例使用 GPT-6.1 Sol，你登录的账户必须有权使用此模型。若没有访问权限，请省略 <code>model</code>，改用你已配置的默认模型。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">各方案对 GPT-6.1 Sol 的访问权限</a>。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-python\">from openai_codex import Codex, Sandbox\nwith Codex() as codex:\n    thread = codex.thread_start(\n        model=\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\n        sandbox=Sandbox.workspace_write,\n    )\n    result = thread.run(\"Make a plan to diagnose and fix the CI failures\")\n    print(result.final_response)\n</code></pre> <p>如果你的应用已经采用异步方式运行，请使用 <code>AsyncCodex</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-python\">import asyncio\nfrom openai_codex import AsyncCodex\nasync def main() -&gt; None:\n    async with AsyncCodex() as codex:\n        thread = await codex.thread_start(model=\"gpt-6.1-sol\")\n        result = await thread.run(\"Implement the plan\")\n        print(result.final_response)\nasyncio.run(main())\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"sandbox-presets\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">沙箱预设</h3> <p>创建线程或更改线程后续轮次的文件系统访问权限时，可以使用相同的 <code>Sandbox</code> 预设：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-python\">from openai_codex import Codex, Sandbox\n\nwith Codex() as codex:\n    thread = codex.thread_start(sandbox=Sandbox.workspace_write)\n    thread.run(\"Make the requested change.\")\n    review = thread.run(\"Review the diff only.\", sandbox=Sandbox.read_only)\n</code></pre> <p>可用预设：</p> <ul> <li><code>Sandbox.read_only</code>：读取文件，但不允许写入。</li> <li><code>Sandbox.workspace_write</code>：读取文件，并在工作区及配置的可写根目录中写入文件。</li> <li><code>Sandbox.full_access</code>：不受文件系统访问限制地运行。</li> </ul> <p>如果不指定 <code>sandbox=</code>，app-server 会使用其配置的默认值。传给 <code>run(...)</code> 或 <code>turn(...)</code> 的沙箱设置只适用于该轮次，以及该线程的后续轮次。</p> <p>更多详情请参阅 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/tree/main/sdk/python\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Python 代码库（需联网）</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"codex-sdk\">Codex SDK</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>If you use Codex through Codex CLI, the IDE extension, or Codex cloud, you can also control it programmatically.</p> <p>Use the SDK when you need to:</p> <ul> <li>Control Codex as part of your CI/CD pipeline</li> <li>Create your own agent that can engage with Codex to perform complex engineering tasks</li> <li>Build Codex into your own internal tools and workflows</li> <li>Integrate Codex within your own application</li> </ul> <p>Use the Codex SDK to automate coding tasks, including jobs in CI. Use the <a href=\"#/article/a-341246db376ea9e1\">Codex app server</a> to build custom clients that handle authentication, conversation history, approvals, and streamed agent events.</p> <p>The <code>codex mcp-server</code> command and standalone <code>codex-mcp-server</code> binary have been removed. Use the <a href=\"#/article/a-341246db376ea9e1\">Codex app server</a> for existing integrations.</p> <p>If you have beta access and need repository or change scans with structured security findings and coverage, use the <a href=\"#/article/a-13b97f7316a6bfd5\">Codex Security TypeScript SDK</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"typescript-library\">TypeScript library</h2> <p>The TypeScript library lets your application start, continue, and resume local Codex threads.</p> <p>Use the library server-side; it requires Node.js 18 or later.</p> <h3 id=\"installation\">Installation</h3> <p>To get started, install the Codex SDK using <code>npm</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install @openai/codex-sdk\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"usage\">Usage</h3> <p>Start a thread with Codex and run it with your prompt.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-ts\">\n\nconst codex = new Codex();\nconst thread = codex.startThread();\nconst result = await thread.run(\n  \"Make a plan to diagnose and fix the CI failures\"\n);\n\nconsole.log(result.finalResponse);\n</code></pre> <p>Call <code>run()</code> again to continue on the same thread, or resume a past thread by providing a thread ID.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-ts\">// running the same thread\nconst result = await thread.run(\"Implement the plan\");\n\nconsole.log(result.finalResponse);\n\n// resuming past thread\n\nconst threadId = \"&lt;thread-id&gt;\";\nconst thread2 = codex.resumeThread(threadId);\nconst result2 = await thread2.run(\"Pick up where you left off\");\n\nconsole.log(result2.finalResponse);\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"configuration-overrides\">Configuration overrides</h3> <p>Pass <code>config</code> to set structured Codex configuration. For keys that can't be expressed as dotted paths, use <code>configOverrides</code> to pass raw TOML strings as separate <code>--config</code> arguments:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-ts\">const codex = new Codex({\n  config: { default_permissions: \"audit\" },\n  configOverrides: [\n    'permissions.audit.filesystem={\":root\"=\"read\",\"/path/to/project/.env\"=\"deny\"}',\n  ],\n});\n</code></pre> <p>Raw overrides take precedence over structured <code>config</code>. The SDK applies managed settings such as <code>baseUrl</code> and thread-specific options afterward, so they take precedence over both. These overrides don't change your Codex configuration files.</p> <p>For more details, check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/tree/main/sdk/typescript\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">TypeScript repo (online)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"python-library\">Python library</h2> <p>The Python SDK controls the local Codex app-server over JSON-RPC. It requires Python 3.10 or later. Published SDK builds include a pinned Codex CLI runtime dependency.</p> <h3 id=\"installation_1\">Installation</h3> <p>To install the SDK run:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">pip install openai-codex\n</code></pre> <p>Published SDK builds automatically use their pinned runtime. Pass <code>CodexConfig(codex_bin=...)</code> only when you intentionally want to run against a specific local Codex executable.</p> <p>The Python SDK is available as a stable release. <code>pip install openai-codex</code> installs the latest stable release. Use <code>pip install --pre openai-codex</code> to opt in to newer prerelease builds.</p> <h3 id=\"usage_1\">Usage</h3> <p>Start Codex, create a thread, and run a prompt. The examples use GPT-6.1 Sol, which must be available to your signed-in account. Otherwise, omit <code>model</code> to use your configured default. See <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol availability by plan</a>.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-python\">from openai_codex import Codex, Sandbox\nwith Codex() as codex:\n    thread = codex.thread_start(\n        model=\"gpt-6.1-sol\",\n        sandbox=Sandbox.workspace_write,\n    )\n    result = thread.run(\"Make a plan to diagnose and fix the CI failures\")\n    print(result.final_response)\n</code></pre> <p>Use <code>AsyncCodex</code> when your application is already asynchronous:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-python\">import asyncio\nfrom openai_codex import AsyncCodex\nasync def main() -&gt; None:\n    async with AsyncCodex() as codex:\n        thread = await codex.thread_start(model=\"gpt-6.1-sol\")\n        result = await thread.run(\"Implement the plan\")\n        print(result.final_response)\nasyncio.run(main())\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"sandbox-presets\">Sandbox presets</h3> <p>Use the same <code>Sandbox</code> presets when creating a thread or changing its filesystem access for a later turn:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-python\">from openai_codex import Codex, Sandbox\n\nwith Codex() as codex:\n    thread = codex.thread_start(sandbox=Sandbox.workspace_write)\n    thread.run(\"Make the requested change.\")\n    review = thread.run(\"Review the diff only.\", sandbox=Sandbox.read_only)\n</code></pre> <p>Available presets:</p> <ul> <li><code>Sandbox.read_only</code>: Read files without allowing writes.</li> <li><code>Sandbox.workspace_write</code>: Read files and write inside the workspace and configured writable roots.</li> <li><code>Sandbox.full_access</code>: Run without filesystem access restrictions.</li> </ul> <p>When you omit <code>sandbox=</code>, app-server uses its configured default. A sandbox passed to <code>run(...)</code> or <code>turn(...)</code> applies to that turn and later turns on the thread.</p> <p>For more details, check out the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/codex/tree/main/sdk/python\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Python repo (online)</a>.</p>"};
